---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../consts';
---

<Page
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="ProofNews privacy policy: what data we collect (very little) and how it is used."
	eyebrow="Legal"
>
	<p>
		ProofNews is a static website. We do not run user accounts, comments, newsletters, or
		analytics trackers of our own — so there is very little personal data for us to collect in
		the first place. This policy explains what little is involved when you visit.
	</p>

	<h2>Information We Collect</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Contact emails.</strong> If you email us or use the contact form (which opens your
			email app), we receive the name, email address, and message content you choose to send.
			We use it only to respond to you.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Server logs.</strong> Our hosting provider may automatically log basic technical
			information such as IP addresses and requested pages for security and operational
			purposes. We do not use this to identify you.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Cookies & Advertising</h2>
	<p>
		ProofNews does not set its own cookies and does not currently use analytics cookies. If we
		display advertising on the Site (for example through Google AdSense), the following applies:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits
			to this website and/or other websites.
		</li>
		<li>
			Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based
			on your visit to our site and/or other sites on the Internet.
		</li>
		<li>
			You may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting
			<a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>.
			Alternatively, you can opt out of a third-party vendor's use of cookies for personalized
			advertising by visiting
			<a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices" rel="noopener">www.aboutads.info/choices</a>.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		Learn more about
		<a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener"
			>how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a
		>.
	</p>

	<h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>External links.</strong> Following a link to another website is subject to that
			site's own privacy practices.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Data Retention & Your Rights</h2>
	<p>
		Emails you send us are kept only as long as needed to handle your inquiry. You may request a
		copy or deletion of any personal information you have sent us by emailing
		<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
	<p>
		This Site is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal
		information from children. If you believe a child has sent us personal information, please
		contact us and we will delete it.
	</p>

	<h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
	<p>
		We may update this policy from time to time. The current version will always be posted on
		this page.
	</p>

	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>
		Questions about this policy? Email us at
		<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
	</p>
</Page>
